&gt; On Fri, Mar 8, 2013 at 4:16 PM, Ben Goodrich &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel="nofollow">goodri...@gmail.com</a> &lt;mailto:<a href data-email-masked rel="nofollow">goodri...@gmail.com</a>&gt;&gt; wrote:<br>&gt;<br>&gt;     On Friday, March 8, 2013 12:04:45 PM UTC-5, Jiqiang Guo wrote:<br>&gt;<br>&gt;         For those who came across this issue, please provide us some more details including<br>&gt;         * the version of R<br>&gt;         * R-Gui, R from the command line, or RStudio (which version)<br>&gt;         * Operating system (Mac, Linux, or Windows)<br>&gt;<br>&gt;         If we are able to reproduce this problem, we could figure out what is the cause though I don&#39;t think it is a<br>&gt;         problem with rstan 1.2.0.<br>&gt;<br>&gt;         --<br>&gt;         Jiqiang<br>&gt;<br>&gt;<br>&gt;         On Fri, Mar 8, 2013 at 12:49 AM, Bob Carpenter &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel="nofollow">ca...@alias-i.com</a>&gt; wrote:<br>&gt;<br>&gt;             More than one user has reported off list that there<br>&gt;             are problems with 404 warnings installing RStan 1.2.0,<br>&gt;             which look as follows<br>&gt;<br>&gt;              &gt; install.packages(&#39;rstan&#39;, type = &#39;source&#39;)<br>&gt;              &gt; Warning in install.packages :<br>&gt;              &gt;    cannot open: HTTP status was &#39;404 Not Found&#39;<br>&gt;<br>&gt;<br>&gt;     This appears to be an RStudio only thing because it overwrites the install.packages function with<br>&gt;<br>&gt;     |<br>&gt;      &gt; install.packages<br>&gt;     function(...) .rs.callAs(name,<br>&gt;                                                                   hook,<br>&gt;                                                                   original,<br>&gt;                                                                   ...)<br>&gt;     &lt;environment: 0x3ac9a70&gt;<br>&gt;      &gt; .rs.callAs<br>&gt;     function(name, f, ...)<br>&gt;     {<br>&gt;         # TODO: figure out how to print the args (...) as part of the message<br>&gt;<br>&gt;         # run the original function (f). setup condition handlers soley so that<br>&gt;         # we can correctly print the name of the function called in error<br>&gt;         # and warning messages -- otherwise R prints &quot;original(...)&quot;<br>&gt;         withCallingHandlers(tryCatch(f(...),<br>&gt;                                      error=function(e)<br>&gt;                                      {<br>&gt;                                         cat(&quot;Error in &quot;, name, &quot; : &quot;, e$message,<br>&gt;                                             &quot;
&quot;, sep=&quot;&quot;)<br>&gt;                                      }),<br>&gt;                             warning=function(w)<br>&gt;                             {<br>&gt;                                cat(&quot;Warning in &quot;, name, &quot; :
  &quot;,  w$message,<br>&gt;                                    &quot;
&quot;, sep=&quot;&quot;)<br>&gt;                                invokeRestart(&quot;muffleWarning&quot;)<br>&gt;                             })<br>&gt;     }<br>&gt;     &lt;environment: 0x374e908&gt;<br>&gt;     |<br>&gt;<br>&gt;     And I imagine the invokeRestart() explains why it subsequently installs. I would guess it is just a flaky internet<br>&gt;     connection or flaky server thing.<br>&gt;<br>&gt;     Ben<br>&gt;<br>&gt;<br>&gt;     --<br>&gt;     You received this message because you are subscribed to the Google Groups &quot;stan development mailing list&quot; group.<br>&gt;     To unsubscribe from this group and stop receiving emails from it, send an email to<br>
